   "H.F3p.K3RM": [
    "Buskin's theorem on S alone reaches only the isometries +-1 of T(S); the classes of K need Hodge isometries through K3 surfaces S' with T(S') = T(S)(c) over Q, known for the general member of certain four-dimensional families (Varesco 2023) and not for the very general member of the eight-dimensional family of real quadratic multiplication"
   ],
   "YM.window.box": [
    "the gauge Dobrushin-Shlosman test needs a box of side about 90 in 4D (4Y-M); no exact computation over SU(2)^{4 n^4} at that size exists"
   ],
   "YM.lattice": [
